Keep in mind, a helm of brilliance can only be safely enchanted to +5 
(but stop enchanting it once it hits +4!) for a total +6 AC at max safe 
enchantment. Wizards (and ONLY Wizards) can safely enchant a cornuthaum 
to +7 (which is also its AC at that enchantment), so a cornuthaum gives 
Wizards 1 more AC point than a HoBrilliance, assuming both are at the 
maximum safe enchantment.

Also, there are the non-AC-related aspects to consider: A HoBrilliance 
gives +5 INT and WIS at max safe enchantment, and provides some 
protection from falling rock traps and boulders from a non-blessed 
scroll of earth; a cornuthaum provides extrinsic clairvoyance and +1 
CHA for a Wizard, and can provide MC2 for a large or huge armor-wearing 
pet (they're too big for anything that provides MC3). Orcish wizards 
will need a HoBrilliance for hungerless casting, but other races can 
get that (and low failure rates overall) without it.


